# Pull request style

Pull requests are the context trail for people and AI agents who read this repo later. This follows pstack's "Opening a PR" playbook (https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack), plus a few house additions.

- **Small:** one script, rule, or skill plus its test. Aim for under about 200 changed lines. Five narrow pull requests beat one fat one.
- **Title:** plain words that say what changed. No "N of M" numbering and no `type(scope):` prefix.
- **Open it ready for review**, not as a draft. A person still reviews and merges every one.
- **Body:** under about 200 words. Use these sections and drop any with nothing to say:
  - **Why:** the problem in one or two sentences.
  - **What changed:** 3 to 6 bullets.
  - **Scope:** what is deliberately left out.
  - **Blast radius:** what else this could affect.
  - **Verification:** the exact command you ran and its result.
- Write short, full sentences in plain words. Explain any label the first time it appears.
- Refer to other pull requests by number (#3), not by their place in a plan. Later fixes get their own pull request.
